  "articleBody": "After a big wind storm, it's natural to want to check your roof for damage right away. But hold on a second! Jumping in without knowing a few key things can actually make things worse, or at least complicate your repair and insurance process. Here at Discounted Roofing Co., we’ve seen some common missteps homeowners make, and we want to help you avoid them.\n\nOne of the biggest mistakes is walking on a damaged roof without proper safety controls. This is incredibly dangerous, especially if there are hidden hazards or unstable areas. Always prioritize safety! Another frequent error is inspecting your roof before clearing hazards like downed power lines, unstable trees, or structural instability. You need to confirm the property is safe first. Don't rush into permanent repairs before you've thoroughly documented all the damage with photos and videos. Your insurance company will need this evidence, and once repairs start, it's hard to prove the original extent of the storm's impact.\n\nMany homeowners assume that missing shingles are the only issue, but wind damage can be much more subtle. It can affect flashing, decking, ventilation, and even the framing underneath. A thorough inspection needs to look beyond just the surface. Lastly, failing to record pre-existing conditions or prior maintenance can hinder your insurance claim. Insurers want to see what's new damage versus old wear and tear. A good assessment clearly separates storm-related damage from routine maintenance issues or aging, which is something we make sure to do in our evaluations.\n\n### Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n**Walking on a damaged roof unsafely:** Never go on a roof without proper safety equipment and training, especially after a storm. It's just too risky.\n\n**Inspecting before hazards are cleared:** Downed lines, unstable trees, or structural issues must be addressed before anyone attempts to inspect the roof.\n\n**Making permanent repairs without documenting damage:** Always take wide and close-up photos or videos of all damage *before* any cleanup or repair work begins for insurance purposes.\n\n**Assuming missing shingles are the only problem:** Wind can cause hidden damage to flashing, decking, ventilation, and more. A comprehensive inspection is key.\n\n**Failing to record pre-existing conditions:** Documenting your roof's condition before the storm can help clarify what's new damage versus old wear and tear for your insurance claim.\n\nWhen a storm hits, stay safe and let the experts handle the assessment. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. today to ensure your roof evaluation is done right.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}